### SQL Queries & Implementation

Below are the cleaned, production-ready SQL queries for each task of the hotel operations analysis.

#### Task 1: Data Cleaning & Type Casting (`branch` table)
Identifies and replaces invalid/missing values, standardizes dirty strings, and casts data types safely using standard ANSI SQL.

```sql
SELECT 
    id,
    -- Handle missing or out-of-scope location categories
    CASE 
        WHEN location IS NULL OR location = '' OR location NOT IN ('EMEA', 'NA', 'LATAM', 'APAC') THEN 'Unknown'
        ELSE location 
    END AS location,
    
    -- Clean total_rooms and ensure integer data type
    CASE 
        WHEN total_rooms IS NULL OR CAST(total_rooms AS numeric) < 1 OR CAST(total_rooms AS numeric) > 400 THEN 100
        ELSE CAST(total_rooms AS integer) 
    END AS total_rooms,
    
    -- Impute missing staff_count based on total_rooms logic (1.5 multiplier)
    CASE 
        WHEN staff_count IS NULL THEN 
            CAST((CASE WHEN total_rooms IS NULL OR CAST(total_rooms AS numeric) < 1 OR CAST(total_rooms AS numeric) > 400 THEN 100 ELSE CAST(total_rooms AS numeric) END) * 1.5 AS numeric)
        ELSE CAST(staff_count AS numeric) 
    END AS staff_count,
    
    -- Handle string placeholders ('-') and filter invalid opening years
    CASE 
        WHEN opening_date IS NULL OR opening_date = '-' OR opening_date = '' OR CAST(opening_date AS integer) < 2000 OR CAST(opening_date AS integer) > 2023 THEN 2023
        ELSE CAST(opening_date AS integer) 
    END AS opening_date,
    
    -- Fix typos ('B.', 'Busniess') using string matching
    CASE 
        WHEN target_guests LIKE 'B%' THEN 'Business'
        WHEN target_guests LIKE 'L%' THEN 'Leisure'
        ELSE 'Leisure' 
    END AS target_guests
FROM branch;
